  <KeyTakeaways
    items={[
      'Bardet–Biedl syndrome (BBS) is a rare, multi-organ inherited disorder: retinal degeneration, obesity, extra digits, kidney anomalies, and learning and reproductive differences.',
      'It is a ciliopathy — a disease of the primary cilium, the antenna almost every cell uses to sense its environment — caused by mutations in the genes that build the BBSome.',
      'Its obesity is a melanocortin problem by a back door: the appetite neurons’ leptin and melanocortin receptors must sit on the cilium, and the broken BBSome never delivers them there.',
